      definition_catalyst: 'Water is your Mind, and as a catalyst, it is how you refill: quiet intake, reading, long conversations, time alone that lets impressions settle into understanding. Your thinking improves in direct proportion to your rest.\n\nReflective, absorbent, better after silence. The best ideas surface in the shower, on the walk, in the hour nobody needed anything, and a rushed week leaves you strangely stupid in ways sleep alone does not fix.\n\nUnderstanding arrives on its own schedule and only through an open door. Hold one screen-free hour before bed. Take the walk before the decision. Keep a note of what surfaces there, because it will be the truest thinking you do.',
